    "description": "Verse-numbering divergence facts across the three shipped riwayat. Translations are keyed to the primary riwayah (Hafs / Kufan numbering); Warsh and Qaloon follow Madinan numbering and partition the same Quranic text differently in the surahs listed below. This file enumerates count divergences derived from surahs.json — it is a checks anchor, NOT a scholarly per-ayah equivalence table. Per-ayah Kufan-Madinan boundary mapping requires authoritative input and is not yet provided.",
    "scholarlySource": {
      "primary": "Abu 'Amr al-Dani (d. 444 AH), 'Al-Bayan fi 'Adad Ay al-Qur'an' — the canonical Sunni reference cataloguing every Kufan / Madinan / Basran / Shami / Makkan verse-counting boundary. Available only as printed / scanned manuscript; no machine-readable per-ayah alias table is in public circulation as of 2026-04. Future per-ayah extension of this file should transcribe al-Dani's chapter-by-chapter splits into a `verseAliases` block.",
      "secondary": "King Fahd Glorious Qur'an Printing Complex (KFGQPC) Madinah Mushaf marginalia — the printed Mushaf marks Kufan splits with marginal indicators ('ك' for kūfī, 'م' for madanī, etc.) on each diverging ayah."
    },
